Y2Kit - readmeThis is a group of utilities designed to fix the problems createdby rbf failing to handle the year 2000 correctly and to eliminatethe problem in the future.  This archive contains the followingfiles:          - kreider.msg which contains instructions on how to            patch Microware's rbf to set file dates to the            year using a base of 1900. i.e. 1999 is 99, 2000            is 100, etc.          - setyear is a utility to set the year to 2000 or            any other year.  It is designed to get around the            input data limitations of Microware's setime.          - fixyear is a utility which checks if the modification            year on a file is < 70 and if so, it adds 100 to the            year.  This utility can be use to clean up the dates            an unpatched rbf leaves behind.          - fixdates is a sh script, i.e. a bash based script,            which allows fixyear to be run on a directory tree.	  - setime2.c this is a clone of Microware's setime	    utility which can handle dates after 1999.          Source code and executables are included in the archive          Use of these utilities is at your own risk.	  Ken Drexler (kdrexler@svn.net)